---
import Layout from '@ui/layouts/Layout.astro';
import { site } from '@core/config/site';
---

<Layout title="How Studely scores offers" description="How Studely scores student offers against fixed, visible criteria — with every point explained.">
  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap prose">
      <p class="eyebrow">Trust &amp; methodology</p>
      <h1>How Studely scores offers</h1>
      <p class="lead">Anyone can paste a list of links. Ours are ranked by a score you can see the reasoning for — not a gut feeling.</p>

      <h2>1. Eligibility, spelled out</h2>
      <p>Every offer shows exactly who can use it and how to prove you’re a student — a <code>.edu</code> email, SheerID, ISIC, or the provider’s own student program. If the eligibility path isn’t clear, it isn’t listed.</p>

      <h2>2. The Studely score</h2>
      <p>Each offer gets a score from 1 to 10, built from fixed, named criteria across three axes: <strong>what you get</strong>, <strong>how hard it is to claim</strong>, and <strong>how long it lasts</strong>. Every offer starts at a neutral 5; each named reason adds or subtracts a small amount, and the result is clamped to 1–10.</p>
      <p>The point of this is honesty: on every offer’s page we show the full breakdown — <em>“full paid tier, free +2”</em>, <em>“no card required +1”</em>, <em>“credit expires −1”</em> — so the ranking is explainable, and you can disagree with a specific reason rather than a mystery number.</p>

      <h2>3. Link checks</h2>
      <p>Automated link checks flag anything broken, redirected or expired for editorial review. That is a backstop against rot, not a guarantee: we don’t claim an offer is live at the moment you click it.</p>

      <h2>4. Honesty about money</h2>
      <p>{site.affiliateDisclosure} Sponsored placements are always labelled <strong>Sponsored</strong>. A payment never buys a better score — only a position.</p>

      <h2>Found something wrong?</h2>
      <p>Offers change fast. If a deal is dead or the terms moved, tell us and we’ll review it. Always confirm current terms on the provider’s own site before relying on an offer.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
